
══════ Cenário 06 — Queda de uma instância da API ══════
(2026-11-23T22:06:41Z)
  POST /auth/login -> HTTP 200

▶ 1. Situação normal: o nginx distribui os pedidos (round-robin)
  GET /accounts -> HTTP 200 (X-Served-By: api-1)
  GET /accounts -> HTTP 200 (X-Served-By: api-2)
  GET /accounts -> HTTP 200 (X-Served-By: api-1)
  GET /accounts -> HTTP 200 (X-Served-By: api-2)
  ✔ respostas: 2×api-1 2×api-2 

▶ 2. Derrubar a api-1
  $ docker stop api-1
  ✔ api-1 parada
  GET /accounts -> HTTP 200 (X-Served-By: api-2)
  GET /accounts -> HTTP 200 (X-Served-By: api-2)
  GET /accounts -> HTTP 200 (X-Served-By: api-2)
  GET /accounts -> HTTP 200 (X-Served-By: api-2)
  GET /accounts -> HTTP 200 (X-Served-By: api-2)
  GET /accounts -> HTTP 200 (X-Served-By: api-2)
  ✔ todos os pedidos responderam 200: 6×api-2 
  logs do nginx: o 1.º pedido tentou a api-1 (172.28.0.11), falhou e foi repetido na api-2 (172.28.0.12);
  depois disso a api-1 fica marcada em baixo durante fail_timeout=10s e nem é tentada:
    2026/11/23 22:06:44 [error] 30#30: *270 upstream timed out (110: Operation timed out) while connecting to upstream, client: 172.28.0.192, server: nginx.global.local, request: "GET /accounts HTTP/1.1", upstream: "https://172.28.0.11:8000/accounts", host: "localhost"
    {"ts":"2026-11-23T22:06:44+00:00","service":"nginx","request_id":"d17fddc5492a1f28566865aa583a0092","method":"GET","uri":"/accounts","status":200,"upstream":"172.28.0.11:8000, 172.28.0.12:8000","upstream_status":"504, 200","ms":2.022}

▶ 3. Voltar a ligar a api-1
  $ docker start api-1
  ✔ api-1 está healthy
  GET /accounts -> HTTP 200 (X-Served-By: api-2)
  GET /accounts -> HTTP 200 (X-Served-By: api-2)
  GET /accounts -> HTTP 200 (X-Served-By: api-1)
  GET /accounts -> HTTP 200 (X-Served-By: api-2)
  GET /accounts -> HTTP 200 (X-Served-By: api-1)
  GET /accounts -> HTTP 200 (X-Served-By: api-2)
  ✔ respostas: 2×api-1 4×api-2 

══════ Cenário 06 concluído: nenhum pedido falhou ══════
